  "work": {
    "abstract_text": "We answer Problem 5.6 of Aivazidis, Loukaki and Müller in the negative (J. Group Theory 27 (2024), p. 1281): the product of the weights f(m)=m!/m^m does not determine a finite set of distinct integers greater than one. The same example answers arXiv:2209.00986v1, Problem 12.6, and v2, Problem 5.6. The two disjoint eighteen-element sets have equal products and equal parameter sums. Their equality follows from the adjacent-weight identity f(n+1)/f(n)=(n/(n+1))^n and an explicit prime-exponent table. For every cardinality at least nineteen, infinitely many rational values have two distinct representations with equal cardinalities and equal sums.",
